## Choose the workflow

- For a clearly requested local fix with no public contract, migration or architectural change, start with `$implement`. Add a regression test and run `make check`. Use the request and the test as the review reference.
- For a change to a public API, event or data contract, a migration, or an architectural decision, use `$specify` and `$plan` and get the resulting spec and plan approved before implementation.
- Use `$discovery` when the problem or desired product outcome needs definition. Clarify ambiguous requirements before writing code.

### Planned changes

| Phase | Skill | Output | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Discovery | `$discovery` | `docs/product/<slug>.md` (PRD) | Human approves problem & metrics |
| 2. Specify | `$specify` | `docs/specs/NNN-<slug>/spec.md` | Human approves acceptance criteria |
| 3. Plan | `$plan` | `docs/specs/NNN-<slug>/plan.md` (+ ADR if needed) | Human approves plan |
| 4. Implement | `$implement` (`$integrate` for new I/O) | Code + tests, one task at a time | `make check` green |
| 5. Review | `$review` | Review report, fixes | No blocking findings |
| 6. Ship | `$ship` | Merge with green CI; follow enabled delivery jobs | With CD enabled, verify the deployed version and readiness |

